  "facts": [
    "The East Channel Bridge opened on November 10, 1923, becoming the first bridge to reach Mercer Island and marking a pivotal moment in the island’s connectivity to the mainland.",
    "In 1940, the original 1923 span was demolished and replaced, paving the way for modern infrastructure that would later support both vehicular traffic and recreational trails.",
    "Today, two parallel steel box girder bridges—one built in 1981 for westbound I‑90 and the I‑90 Trail, the other in 1988 for eastbound I‑90 and the 2 Line light rail—carry the island’s bustling traffic."
